Photos are back on the widget. Large shots did not fit into the memory the system gives a widget, so it died before drawing anything — an empty rectangle on the home screen, while the photo sat fine inside the app. Both Android and iPhone, and the better the camera, the worse it got.

The widget got twice as light. A photo is now scaled by its longer side, not the shorter one: the pair widget holds two halves plus avatars, and together they used to hit the memory ceiling.

If a photo cannot be scaled, the previous one stays. Before, the original went to the widget as is — and the widget went dark.

An empty widget now says its own name. "Partner's photo" was labelled "Photo of the day · No memories" and looked like someone else's, so people thought it had not been added and kept adding more.
